    13| *   2. Strategic planner — 30-day / 90-day / yearly goals derived from gaps.
    14| *   3. Opportunity engine — detected leads / investors / customers, ranked.
    15| *   4. Decision engine — recommended actions with estimated impact + risk.
    16| *   5. Execution tracking — what was planned / executed / remains.
    17| *   6. Executive dashboard — company / AI / engineering / capital scorecards.
    18| *
    19| * HARD HONESTY RULES (inherited from the engines it composes):
    20| *   - Never promise guaranteed profit; upside is "potential", always caveated.
    21| *   - Cash runway requires burn/expense data IVX does NOT track → reported as
    22| *     `unknown` with the exact missing input, never a fabricated number.
    23| *   - Every figure is grounded in a real subsystem record; an empty source
    24| *     reads as 0 / null with an honest note.
    25| *
    26| * Deterministic + defensive: pure derivations over already-collected dashboards.
    27| * Each source is gathered defensively so one failed reader degrades to an
    28| * honest empty value, never throws.
